      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/3e35d57afedf09a31233e1c10488dc43f4680ed9/vllm%2Fmodel_executor%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fcompressed_tensors%2Fcompressed_tensors.py",
      "changes": 8,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/vllm%2Fmodel_executor%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fcompressed_tensors%2Fcompressed_tensors.py?ref=3e35d57afedf09a31233e1c10488dc43f4680ed9",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "vllm/model_executor/layers/quantization/compressed_tensors/compressed_tensors.py",
      "patch": "@@ -288,7 +288,13 @@ def _parse_sparsity_config(\n         sparsity_ignore_list = sparsity_config.ignore or list()\n \n         # Raise DeprecationError if non-empty sparse_scheme_map is detected\n-        if sparse_scheme_map:\n+        # A ``format: dense`` sparsity_config carries only vestigial sparsity\n+        # metadata (weights are stored dense) and loads fine as a normal\n+        # quantized model, so only reject actually-sparse (compressed) formats.\n+        if (\n+            sparse_scheme_map\n+            and sparsity_config.format != CompressionFormat.dense.value\n+        ):\n             raise DeprecationWarning(\n                 \"Sparsity support has been removed from compressed-tensors. \"\n                 \"Please use a model without sparsity configuration.\"",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/3e35d57afedf09a31233e1c10488dc43f4680ed9/vllm%2Fmodel_executor%2Flayers%2Fquantization%2Fcompressed_tensors%2Fcompressed_tensors.py",
      "sha": "0a33cc259f3dcb7e94475b2f72d48419f09c12a9",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Clarification on scope: this only affects models built with an **older version of compressed-tensors**.\r\n\r\n- compressed-tensors [#610](https://github.com/vllm-project/compressed-tensors/pull/610) (merged 2026-03-17) removed sparse-compression support and stopped writing `sparsity_config` on save, so models produced since then don't carry this field and are unaffected. (An earlier attempt to suppress the dense config, [#169](https://github.com/vllm-project/compressed-tensors/pull/169), was reverted by [#181](https://github.com/vllm-project/compressed-tensors/pull/181), so models produced from late-2024 through early-2026 — e.g. `RedHatAI/granite-3.1-8b-instruct-quantized.w4a16` — still have a vestigial `format: dense` `sparsity_config`.)\r\n\r\nThe field is being scrubbed from affected checkpoints at the source, but this fix is still worthwhile:\r\n\r\n- **Already-published checkpoints are in users' hands.** Re-saving a model upstream can't fix copies people have already downloaded/pinned; this makes them load as-is.\r\n- **It's a correctness fix, not a workaround.** `format: dense` genuinely means the weights are stored dense (verified: the affected models' recipes apply quantization only, and their safetensors contain standard pack-quantized tensors with zero sparse-storage artifacts). `from_config` already discards the parsed sparse scheme map, so the raise was rejecting ordinary quantized models. Genuinely-sparse (compressed) formats are still rejected.\r\n",
      "created_at": "2026-08-05T19:17:54Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51189#issuecomment-5196259468",
      "id": 5196259468,
